---
/**
 * The four boxes any yes/no detector fills in, arranged as what the test said
 * against what was actually true.
 *
 * The teaching load is carried by the words in each box, not by the tint: both
 * mistake boxes say MISTAKE, both correct boxes say RIGHT, and the two mistakes
 * are additionally outlined in a broken line while the two correct ones are
 * solid. Strip the colour out entirely and every distinction survives
 * (hard rule 9). The bottom-right box says in words that nearly everybody lands
 * in it, which is the whole reason accuracy can look so good — that sentence,
 * rather than a colour, is what makes the point.
 *
 * Decorative by itself, so `aria-hidden`: `Figure` supplies the accessible name
 * and the description.
 */
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 640 322" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
  <!-- Column headings: what was actually true. -->
  <g class="fill-ink font-display" font-size="14" font-weight="700">
    <text x="294" y="32" text-anchor="middle">Actually ill</text>
    <text x="522" y="32" text-anchor="middle">Actually healthy</text>
  </g>

  <!-- Row headings: what the test said. -->
  <g class="fill-ink font-display" font-size="12" font-weight="600">
    <text x="168" y="100" text-anchor="end">The test raises</text>
    <text x="168" y="115" text-anchor="end">the alarm</text>
    <text x="168" y="220" text-anchor="end">The test stays</text>
    <text x="168" y="235" text-anchor="end">quiet</text>
  </g>

  <!-- Top left: the alarm was worth raising. -->
  <rect
    x="184"
    y="48"
    width="220"
    height="112"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-success-soft stroke-rule-strong"
    stroke-width="1.25"></rect>
  <text x="198" y="70" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="9"
    >RIGHT</text
  >
  <text
    x="198"
    y="98"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="15"
    font-weight="700">Caught it</text
  >
  <text x="198" y="120" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >Somebody ill was found</text
  >
  <text x="198" y="134" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >while there was still time.</text
  >

  <!-- Top right: a mistake, and the cheaper one here. -->
  <rect
    x="412"
    y="48"
    width="220"
    height="112"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-danger-soft stroke-danger"
    stroke-width="1.25"
    stroke-dasharray="4 4"></rect>
  <text x="426" y="70" class="fill-danger font-mono" font-size="9">MISTAKE</text
  >
  <text
    x="426"
    y="98"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="15"
    font-weight="700">False alarm</text
  >
  <text x="426" y="120" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >Nothing was there. A</text
  >
  <text x="426" y="134" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >frightening fortnight,</text
  >
  <text x="426" y="148" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >and another test.</text
  >

  <!-- Bottom left: a mistake, and the expensive one here. -->
  <rect
    x="184"
    y="168"
    width="220"
    height="112"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-danger-soft stroke-danger"
    stroke-width="1.25"
    stroke-dasharray="4 4"></rect>
  <text x="198" y="190" class="fill-danger font-mono" font-size="9"
    >MISTAKE</text
  >
  <text
    x="198"
    y="218"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="15"
    font-weight="700">Missed it</text
  >
  <text x="198" y="240" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >Sent home reassured.</text
  >
  <text x="198" y="254" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >Nobody looks again</text
  >
  <text x="198" y="268" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >until much later.</text
  >

  <!-- Bottom right: correct, and enormous. -->
  <rect
    x="412"
    y="168"
    width="220"
    height="112"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-success-soft stroke-rule-strong"
    stroke-width="1.25"></rect>
  <text x="426" y="190" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="9"
    >RIGHT</text
  >
  <text
    x="426"
    y="218"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="15"
    font-weight="700">Left alone, correctly</text
  >
  <text x="426" y="240" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >Almost everybody who</text
  >
  <text x="426" y="254" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10"
    >walks in lands in this</text
  >
  <text x="426" y="268" class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="10">one box.</text>

  <g class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="11">
    <text x="8" y="300"
      >Accuracy adds the two boxes marked RIGHT together, and says nothing about</text
    >
    <text x="8" y="314"
      >which mistake you are making. When the hunted thing is rare, the
      bottom-right box is nearly all of the score.</text
    >
  </g>
</svg>
